  "details": "This issue has been present for a long time and still hasn't been fixed. There is a mismatch between remote and local hand tracking, which is especially important for sign language communication.\n\nIn the first picture (remote view, as seen by a friend), I am making the \"C\" sign. However, in the second picture (my local view), the hand pose is completely different and looks like I'm making a \"duck\" gesture instead.\n\nAccurate hand tracking across both views is essential for consistent gestures and sign language interpretation.",
